From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:58:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0070 -- fold SDL/0146's GUS voice-setup cost
 diagnostic into AUDIOPRB.LOG (S7-GUS)

Same rollup-of-rollups pattern as patch 0069's own gusscan fold-in:
snapshots SDL_DOSGusSetVoiceFreqDiagSnapshot/SetVoiceVolDiagSnapshot/
SetVoicePanDiagSnapshot/StartVoiceDiagSnapshot/StopVoiceDiagSnapshot
once per audio_core_entry_poll() poll() call, discard-snapshotting
first (same attribution-correctness reasoning as the OPL3 regwrite and
GUS-scan discards) so a call triggered outside this function's own slot
loop is never misattributed. Adds five new fields to the existing
DOS-PORT audioprb log line: voicefreq, voicevol, voicepan, voicestart,
voicestop (calls/min_us/mean_us/max_us each) -- one per SDL patch
SDL/0146 accessor, kept independent (not combined into one aggregate)
so the real-hardware result can attribute the ~6.89s slots_us outlier
to a specific function rather than just their combined total.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VVzc2V3qXnVbYZC693CTWt
